# Claude Supervisor environment
#
# Copy to ~/.claude-supervisor/.env (mode 600, owned by the user running the
# service — `sashi` on the live host) and fill in real values.
# NEVER commit this file with real values. It is not tracked in this repo —
# only the .example template is.

# Claude — called via the `claude` (Claude Code) CLI, not the Anthropic API,
# so this draws on a Claude subscription's usage rather than metered
# per-token billing. Authenticate the `sashi` user's `claude` install once,
# before starting this service, with EITHER:
#   - `claude login` (interactive, browser OAuth) — fine for a one-time
#     manual step even on a headless box if you can port-forward/tunnel it, or
#   - `claude setup-token` (built for headless/CI use) — VERIFY the exact
#     command and whether it needs an env var set here (e.g.
#     CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN) against `claude setup-token --help`; not
#     independently confirmed from this session.
# If setup-token gives you a token to export, put it here:
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
CLAUDE_SUPERVISOR_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Paperclip — company id from `paperclipai company list` once Paperclip is
# installed (see ../paperclip-hermes/README.md). The value below is what
# OPERATIONS.md claimed before Paperclip was confirmed to not be installed
# yet — verify it's still correct once the real install exists, don't trust
# it blindly.
PAPERCLIP_API_KEY=
PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID=0c265070-3974-497a-99ee-cf942ffe139d

# claude-supervisor's own Paperclip agent identity must exist before
# PAPERCLIP_API_KEY above can be minted (`paperclipai agent create` +
# `paperclipai token agent create` — see README.md "Manual setup"). The
# daemon doesn't need the agent id itself at runtime; the API key alone
# carries its identity to Paperclip.

# Poll behavior
POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=300

# Local repo paths, used only for a best-effort git-log lookup (read-only,
# never written to)
IBMIMCP_REPO_PATH=/home/sashi/Documents/projects/RSA/IBMiMCP
INOVA_REPO_PATH=/home/sashi/Documents/projects/RSA/inova
FLEET_REPO_PATH=/home/sashi/Documents/projects/RSA/always-on-engineering-fleet
